        "tree_id": "9d247f5331b6863f6dccecaebd82daf5651385e7",
        "message": "fix(ci): py3.11 f-string backslash in hedioum yml render + useradd guard\n\n- ssh_family HedioumAdapter._yml rebuilt with %-formatting: the old\n  f-string embedded escaped quotes (backslash) inside the expression,\n  which Python 3.11 rejects (allowed only from 3.12) — broke CI matrix\n- install.sh second-run idempotency: 'id -r USER' is invalid POSIX\n  without -u/-g (always non-zero), so useradd ran every time and failed\n  when the user existed; guard is now plain 'id tunnelpannel'\n- CI now also AST-gates canonical sources for py3.11 compatibility\n  (checked locally; matrix enforces it)",
